  "rules": "Auto memo date and capture order, one rule set for every client (memos-ng SPA, memos-ng-ios) and for the server's capture read.\nF1 DATE. Auto is the EARLIEST eligible capture instant among the memo's attached photos and videos, compared as integer epoch SECONDS; media without an eligible instant is ignored; none at all means 'now' (the client omits created_at). A civil time (F2, no offset) is resolved by the CLIENT in one explicit IANA zone and competes on its resolved seconds like any other; when the winner is a civil-resolved one the control marks it approximate. Auto is recomputed on every add, remove, retry and late completion; posting waits until every retained item's capture decision has SETTLED, whatever the date mode.\nSPAN. When the earliest and the latest eligible instant fall on different calendar days in the DISPLAY zone, the control appends a span of N days, N being the inclusive calendar-day count (1 Jan and 3 Jan is 3; 23:50 and 00:10 the next day is 2); same-day is no hint.\nF1b ORDER. Items with a settled eligible instant come first, ascending by resolved epoch seconds; items without one follow in PICK order; ties are in pick order. That order is what the composer shows and what it sends (upload_uids / the outbox manifest). The server persists it as attachments.position, 0-based in the request, NULL for legacy rows; a memo's attachments read back by position NULLS LAST, then id. Files added on edit are appended after the existing attachments: when ANY existing attachment of the memo has a NULL position, all of them are renumbered 0..k-1 in their current displayed order first; otherwise numbering continues from max + 1. There is no manual reorder in 1.4.\nF2 CAPTURE READ. Images: the PRIMARY image's EXIF DateTimeOriginal (0x9003). With OffsetTimeOriginal (0x9011), or a matching OffsetTime (0x9010), it is an exact instant, source 'exif'; without one it is a CIVIL time 'YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS' (no instant) that the client resolves, source 'exif'. A civil time landing in a DST gap is rejected (the item counts as undated); in an overlap the EARLIER instant wins. SubSecTimeOriginal is ignored \u2014 whole seconds everywhere. Videos: com.apple.quicktime.creationdate (ISO 8601 with offset, from moov/meta keys+ilst) first, source 'quicktime'; else the mvhd creation_time read as UTC seconds since 1904-01-01, REJECTED when zero, before 1990-01-01, or after now + 1 day. No track-level (tkhd/mdhd) fallback. Fractional seconds are floored. Malformed or missing tags yield no instant and never an error. Only the date tags above are read: no GPS, no metadata dumps, no pixel decode. A 'sibling' capture_source is a SERVER-side post-hoc fill from img-manager's index of the RAW original (MEMNG-796); clients compute nothing new and never see a civil time for it.",
